    "basis": "author-died-pre-1930",
    "detail": "Beethoven died in 1827. The Bagatelle in A minor WoO 59 was composed around 1810 and first published in 1867 by Ludwig Nohl; the composition is free worldwide.",
    "sourceEdition": "Beethoven, Bagatelle in A minor WoO 59 (Fur Elise), Nohl 1867 first edition text as carried in the Breitkopf & Hartel complete works",
    "notes": "Original meter is 3/8; encoded at the EIGHTH-NOTE pulse as 3/4, so one encoded beat = one written eighth note and the sixteenth-note figuration sits on the 0.5-beat grid. Carries the famous A minor rondo theme only (mm. 1-17); the F major and demisemiquaver episodes are not encoded. Melody is the standard single-line reduction including the low arpeggio pickup figures. Sections are cut so each ends with the E-D# run bar, so every section boundary resolves onto the A downbeat exactly as in the score. No lyrics (the piece has none)."
  },
